- introduction_notebook_submission.csv

These data files are the property of TNO (Netherlands Organisation for Applied 
Scientific Research) and are provided subject to the following strict conditions:

1. ACADEMIC & NON-COMMERCIAL USE ONLY
   The data may only be used for academic and non-commercial purposes. 
   Commercial use is strictly prohibited.

2. COMPETITION RULES FOR TEST SET
   Access to and use of the test set (`test.csv`, `test.bin`, `debug_introduction_notebook_submission.csv`) is strictly 
   conditional upon agreeing to the terms and rules of the AI Cup 2026 – 
   Performance Track competition. By accessing these files, you acknowledge 
   that you have read and agreed to the rules located at:
   https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/ai-cup-2026-performance/rules, especially section 2.4 Competition Data

   This condition holds until the data is explicitly revealed by the compeition organizers.

3. NO REVERSE ENGINEERING OF TEST SET
   You may not attempt to reverse engineer, de-anonymize, or manually label 
   the test set data. (`test.csv`, `test.bin`, `debug_introduction_notebook_submission.csv`)

   You agree that you use the test data only to calculate, submit and debug submissions for the AI Cup 2026 competition only until the test data, if it happens, is revealed by the competition organizers.

4. ATTRIBUTION REQUIREMENT
   Any use, modification, or distribution of the dataset must include
   clear attribution to the original author:

   © 2026 AI Cup 2026, AIC4NL | Team Epoch
   Dataset provided by TNO (Netherlands Organisation for Applied Scientific Research)

   Attribution must be visible in:
   - Source code distributions (in the LICENSE file), and
   - End-user applications (e.g., in an "About", documentation, or credits section), if applicable.

